# Autonomous development workflow

**Assume this workflow in every new chat.** The user does **not** repeat staging/prod instructions. Follow it end-to-end unless they explicitly override.

Canonical ops doc: `docs/ops/staging-dev.md`  
Makefile: `make help`  
Skill: `.cursor/skills/staging-workflow/SKILL.md`

## This server (fixed facts)

| | Production | Staging |
|---|------------|---------|
| Path | `/opt/bot-remnawave` | same repo |
| Compose | `docker compose` | `docker compose -f docker-compose.staging.yml --env-file .env.staging -p remnawave-staging` |
| Env file | `.env` (gitignored) | `.env.staging` (gitignored) |
| Telegram | prod bot (`@MOONVPN_BOT` or prod `BOT_USERNAME` in `.env`) | **`@mrj7_bot`** |
| Host ports | `8080`, `3020` | **`8081`**, **`3021`** |
| Public URLs | prod `hooks` / `cabinet` on `rookari.com` | **`staging-host-hooks`**, **`staging-host-cabinet`**, **`staging-host-miniapp`**, **`staging-host-sub`** |
| DB host in staging env | — | `POSTGRES_HOST=staging-postgres` (not `postgres`) |
| Bot `WEB_API_PORT` inside container | `8080` | **`8080`** (host maps `8081:8080`) |

**Never** iterate i18n/UX on the production Telegram bot. **Always** smoke on `@mrj7_bot` + staging cabinet URL.

## What the agent does without being asked

### A. New feature / i18n / fix (multi-step)

1. **Plan** — for non-trivial work, write or update `docs/superpowers/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>.md` (phases, files, smoke paths).
2. **Branch** from `main` (`i18n/`, `fix/`, `feat/`, `chore/`).
3. **Implement** — minimal diff; one concern per commit (`localization-upstream.mdc`).
4. **After each commit** — agent smoke:
   ```bash
   make smoke
   make check-admin-texts
   # if cabinet touched: docker compose run --rm --no-deps -w /app/cabinet node:20-alpine sh -c "npm ci && npm run build"
   ```
5. **Commit** when a slice is done (user must ask for commit only if they use that policy; otherwise commit per `delivery-cycle.mdc`).
6. **End of slice or sprint** — deploy **staging in background** (do not block chat on rebuilds):
   ```bash
   make deploy-scope
   make staging-rebuild    # background → /tmp/remnabot-deploy-staging-*.log
   # when log shows success:
   make staging-health
   ```
   Use `make staging-migrate` if new Alembic revision (foreground).
7. **Smoke map** — fill `docs/templates/smoke-map.md` (keys, handlers, Telegram path on `@mrj7_bot`).
8. **Tell user** — short checklist: what to tap in Telegram / which staging URL; ask for smoke sign-off (`تایید` / “approved”).

### B. After user approves staging smoke

User words like **تایید**, **approved**, **smoke OK** = permission to ship. Agent runs **in order** (no re-asking):

```bash
CONFIRM_SHIP=1 make ship BRANCH=<feature-branch>
# PR on remnabot fork:
gh pr merge <number> -R k4lantar4/remnabot --merge
git checkout main && git pull remnabot main
CONFIRM_PROD_DEPLOY=1 make prod-deploy
```

Then report: PR URL, merge sha, prod health hint (`make prod-ps`). User does a **short prod smoke** on live bot.

Use `GITHUB_REPO=k4lantar4/remnabot` for all `gh` commands (default `gh` remote is upstream).

### C. Forbidden without explicit user override

| Action | Rule |
|--------|------|
| `docker compose build/up` on **prod** stack while iterating | Use **staging** only |
| `CONFIRM_PROD_DEPLOY=1` / `make prod-deploy` | Only **after** staging smoke approval + merge to `main` |
| `CONFIRM_SHIP=1` / `make ship` | Only **after** user staging smoke approval |
| `git push remnabot main` / force-push `main` | Never without explicit user request |
| Edit `.env` / `.env.staging` secrets in commits | Never commit secrets |
| `docker compose` without staging flags for UI testing | Wrong stack — use `make staging-*` |

## Makefile quick reference

```bash
make smoke && make deploy-scope && make staging-rebuild   # background staging deploy
make staging-health                                       # after deploy log succeeds
CONFIRM_SHIP=1 make ship BRANCH=i18n/foo                    # after user تایید staging
CONFIRM_PROD_DEPLOY=1 make prod-deploy                      # auto scope, background
CONFIRM_PROD_DEPLOY=1 make prod-deploy-bot                  # explicit bot-only
```

**Agent policy:** always use background deploy (`make staging-rebuild`, `make prod-deploy*`) unless the user asks to wait inline.

